---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
---

<LegalLayout title="Support" description="Help, subscriptions, data controls, and contact information for Dee: Muay Thai Coach.">
  <p class="legal-eyebrow">DEE SUPPORT</p>
  <h1>How can we help?</h1>
  <p class="legal-lede">Dee is built to stay out of the way while you train. If something is not working, the quickest route is usually below.</p>

  <section class="support-grid" aria-label="Support options">
    <a class="support-card" href="mailto:support@dee.training?subject=Dee%20support">
      <span>01</span>
      <h2>Email support</h2>
      <p>Tell us what happened, your device model, and the Dee version shown in Settings.</p>
      <strong>support@dee.training ↗</strong>
    </a>
    <a class="support-card" href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      <span>02</span>
      <h2>Manage a subscription</h2>
      <p>View, change, or cancel Dee Pro through your Apple Account.</p>
      <strong>Apple subscriptions ↗</strong>
    </a>
    <a class="support-card" href="/privacy/#deleting-your-data">
      <span>03</span>
      <h2>Delete your data</h2>
      <p>Use Delete Data in Dee’s Settings to remove your profile, plans, settings, and workout history.</p>
      <strong>Read the details →</strong>
    </a>
  </section>

  <h2>Quick answers</h2>

  <h3>Does Dee need an account?</h3>
  <p>No. Dee does not require a Dee account. Your training data is stored locally; on iOS it may also sync through your private iCloud database when available.</p>

  <h3>Can I train without a signal?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Dee keeps its exercise library and workout player on your device. A built-in plan is available when plan generation cannot run.</p>

  <h3>How do I restore Dee Pro?</h3>
  <p>Open Dee, go to Settings, and use the restore-purchases option. Make sure the device is signed in to the Apple Account that made the purchase.</p>

  <h3>How do I report a problem?</h3>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@dee.training?subject=Dee%20support">support@dee.training</a>. Please include the device, operating-system version, Dee version, what you expected, and what happened. Do not send injury notes or other sensitive information unless it is necessary for your request.</p>

  <h3>Is Dee medical advice?</h3>
  <p>No. Dee is for general sport and fitness. Stop if something feels unsafe and speak to a qualified coach or clinician about technique, pain, injuries, or whether exercise is appropriate for you.</p>
</LegalLayout>
